xref:lookup[$lookup<K, V>(pair<K, V>^{asterisk}^, K~query~)]

. If ``pair<K, V>^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. Return ``·``.
. Else:
 .. Check that ``K~h~`` is equal to ``K~query~``.

 .. Return ``V~h~``.

. Otherwise:
 .. Otherwise:
  ... Check that ``pair<K, V>^{asterisk}^`` is a non-empty list.

  ... Let ``K~h~ → V~h~ {two-colons} ( K~t~ → V~t~ )^{asterisk}^`` be ``pair<K, V>^{asterisk}^``.
  ... Return ``xref:lookup[$lookup<K, V>(( K~t~ → V~t~ )^{asterisk}^, K~query~)]``.

xref:Check_expr[Check_expr: ``tenv ⊢ expr +:+ %``]

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... If let ``literal`` be ``expr``:
   .... If let ``i`` be ``literal``:
    ..... Result in ``+INT+``.
   .... Else:
    ..... Result in ``+BOOL+``.
  ... Else if let ``x`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let ``t`` be xref:option_get[*!*] ``xref:lookup[$lookup<id, type>(tenv, x)]``.
   .... Result in ``t``.
 .. {empty}
  ... If let ``+!+ e`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e +:+ type``].
   .... Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+BOOL+``.

   .... Result in ``+BOOL+``.
  ... Else if let ``e~l~ +++ e~r~`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~l~ +:+ type``].
   .... Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+INT+``.

   .... Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~r~ +:+ type'``].
   .... Check that ``type'`` matches pattern ``+INT+``.

   .... Result in ``+INT+``.
  ... Else if let ``e~l~ +<=+ e~r~`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~l~ +:+ type``].
   .... Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+INT+``.

   .... Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~r~ +:+ type'``].
   .... Check that ``type'`` matches pattern ``+INT+``.

   .... Result in ``+BOOL+``.
  ... Else if let ``e~l~ +&&+ e~r~`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~l~ +:+ type``].
   .... Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+BOOL+``.

   .... Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~r~ +:+ type'``].
   .... Check that ``type'`` matches pattern ``+BOOL+``.

   .... Result in ``+BOOL+``.
  ... Else if let ``e~1~ +?+ e~2~ +:+ e~3~`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~1~ +:+ type``].
   .... Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+BOOL+``.

   .... Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~2~ +:+ t``].
   .... Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~3~ +:+ type'``].
   .... Check that ``type'`` is equal to ``t``.

   .... Result in ``t``.
  ... Else if let ``+FUN+ +(+t~arg~ x~arg~+)+ +->+ t~ret~ +{+e+}+`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let xref:Check_expr[``x~arg~ → t~arg~ {two-colons} tenv ⊢ e +:+ type``].
   .... Check that ``type`` is equal to ``t~ret~``.

   .... Result in ``t~arg~ +->+ t~ret~``.
  ... Else if let ``e~f~ +(+e~a~+)+`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~f~ +:+ type``].
   .... Let!~type~ ``t~arg~ +->+ t~ret~`` be ``type``.

   .... Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~a~ +:+ type'``].
   .... Check that ``type'`` is equal to ``t~arg~``.

   .... Result in ``t~ret~``.

xref:Check_command[Check_command: ``tenv ⊢ command ⊣ %``]

. If ``command`` matches pattern ``+SKIP+``:
 .. Result in ``tenv``.
. Else if let ``t x +=+ e`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e +:+ type``].
 .. Check that ``type`` is equal to ``t``.

 .. Result in ``x → t {two-colons} tenv``.
. Else if let ``x +=+ e`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e +:+ t``].
 .. Check that ``xref:lookup[$lookup<id, type>(tenv, x)]`` is equal to ``t``.

 .. Result in ``tenv``.
. Else if let ``+IF+ e +THEN+ c~1~ +ELSE+ c~2~ +END+`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e +:+ type``].
 .. Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+BOOL+``.

 .. Let xref:Check_command[``tenv ⊢ c~1~ ⊣ tenv~1~``].
 .. Let xref:Check_command[``tenv ⊢ c~2~ ⊣ tenv~2~``].
 .. Result in ``tenv``.
. Else if let ``+WHILE+ e +DO+ c +END+`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e +:+ type``].
 .. Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+BOOL+``.

 .. Let xref:Check_command[``tenv ⊢ c ⊣ tenv~1~``].
 .. Result in ``tenv``.
. Else if let ``c~1~ +;+ c~2~`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Check_command[``tenv ⊢ c~1~ ⊣ tenv~1~``].
 .. Let xref:Check_command[``tenv~1~ ⊢ c~2~ ⊣ tenv~2~``].
 .. Result in ``tenv~2~``.
. Else:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``x~arg~ → t~arg~ {two-colons} f → t~arg~ +->+ t~ret~ {two-colons} tenv ⊢ e +:+ type``].
 .. Check that ``type`` is equal to ``t~ret~``.

 .. Result in ``f → t~arg~ +->+ t~ret~ {two-colons} tenv``.

xref:Check_prog[Check_prog: ``⊢ command``]

. Let xref:Check_command[``· ⊢ command ⊣ tenv``].
. The relation holds.

xref:Eval_expr[Eval_expr: ``env ⊢ expr ⟹ %``]

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... If let ``literal`` be ``expr``:
   .... If let ``i`` be ``literal``:
    ..... Result in ``i``.
   .... Else:
    ..... Result in ``b``.
  ... Else if let ``x`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let ``v`` be xref:option_get[*!*] ``xref:lookup[$lookup<id, value>(env, x)]``.
   .... Result in ``v``.
 .. {empty}
  ... If let ``+!+ e`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e ⟹ value``].
   .... Let!~type~ ``literal`` be ``value``.

   .... Let!~type~ ``b~e~`` be ``literal``.

   .... Let ``b`` be not ``b~e~``.
   .... Result in ``b``.
  ... Else if let ``e~l~ +++ e~r~`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~l~ ⟹ value``].
   .... Let!~type~ ``literal`` be ``value``.

   .... Let!~type~ ``i~l~`` be ``literal``.

   .... Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~r~ ⟹ value'``].
   .... Let!~type~ ``literal'`` be ``value'``.

   .... Let!~type~ ``i~r~`` be ``literal'``.

   .... Let ``i`` be ``i~l~`` + ``i~r~``.
   .... Result in ``i``.
  ... Else if let ``e~l~ +<=+ e~r~`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~l~ ⟹ value``].
   .... Let!~type~ ``literal`` be ``value``.

   .... Let!~type~ ``i~l~`` be ``literal``.

   .... Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~r~ ⟹ value'``].
   .... Let!~type~ ``literal'`` be ``value'``.

   .... Let!~type~ ``i~r~`` be ``literal'``.

   .... Let ``b`` be ``i~l~`` is less than or equal to ``i~r~``.
   .... Result in ``b``.
  ... Else if let ``e~l~ +&&+ e~r~`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~l~ ⟹ value``].
   .... Let!~type~ ``literal`` be ``value``.

   .... Let!~type~ ``b~l~`` be ``literal``.

   .... Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~r~ ⟹ value'``].
   .... Let!~type~ ``literal'`` be ``value'``.

   .... Let!~type~ ``b~r~`` be ``literal'``.

   .... Let ``b`` be ``b~l~`` and ``b~r~``.
   .... Result in ``b``.
  ... Else if let ``e~1~ +?+ e~2~ +:+ e~3~`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~1~ ⟹ value``].
   .... Try:
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``true``.

     ...... Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~2~ ⟹ v``].
     ...... Result in ``v``.
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``false``.

     ...... Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~3~ ⟹ v``].
     ...... Result in ``v``.
  ... Else if let ``+FUN+ +(+t~arg~ x~arg~+)+ +->+ t~ret~ +{+e+}+`` be ``expr``:
   .... Result in ``+CLO+ x~arg~ e env``.
  ... Else if let ``e~f~ +(+e~a~+)+`` be ``expr``:
   .... Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~f~ ⟹ value``].
   .... If let ``+CLO+ x~a~ e~body~ env~clo~`` be ``value``:
    ..... Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~a~ ⟹ v``].
    ..... Let xref:Eval_expr[``x~a~ → v {two-colons} env~clo~ ⊢ e~body~ ⟹ v~ret~``].
    ..... Result in ``v~ret~``.
   .... Else if let ``+RECCLO+ f x~arg~ e~body~ env~clo~`` be ``value``:
    ..... Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~a~ ⟹ v``].
    ..... Let xref:Eval_expr[``x~arg~ → v {two-colons} f → +RECCLO+ f x~arg~ e~body~ env~clo~ {two-colons} env~clo~ ⊢ e~body~ ⟹ v~ret~``].
    ..... Result in ``v~ret~``.

xref:Eval_command[Eval_command: ``env ⊢ command ⊣ %``]

. If ``command`` matches pattern ``+SKIP+``:
 .. Result in ``env``.
. Else if let ``t x +=+ e`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e ⟹ v``].
 .. Result in ``x → v {two-colons} env``.
. Else if let ``x +=+ e`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e ⟹ v``].
 .. Result in ``x → v {two-colons} env``.
. Else if let ``+IF+ e +THEN+ c~1~ +ELSE+ c~2~ +END+`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e ⟹ value``].
 .. Try:
  ... {empty}
   .... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``true``.

   .... Let xref:Eval_command[``env ⊢ c~1~ ⊣ env~1~``].
   .... Result in ``env~1~``.
  ... {empty}
   .... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``false``.

   .... Let xref:Eval_command[``env ⊢ c~2~ ⊣ env~2~``].
   .... Result in ``env~2~``.
. Else if let ``+WHILE+ e +DO+ c +END+`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e ⟹ value``].
 .. Try:
  ... {empty}
   .... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``false``.

   .... Result in ``env``.
  ... {empty}
   .... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``true``.

   .... Let xref:Eval_command[``env ⊢ c ⊣ env~1~``].
   .... Let xref:Eval_command[``env~1~ ⊢ +WHILE+ e +DO+ c +END+ ⊣ env~2~``].
   .... Result in ``env~2~``.
. Else if let ``c~1~ +;+ c~2~`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Eval_command[``env ⊢ c~1~ ⊣ env~1~``].
 .. Let xref:Eval_command[``env~1~ ⊢ c~2~ ⊣ env~2~``].
 .. Result in ``env~2~``.
. Else:
 .. Result in ``f → +RECCLO+ f x~arg~ e env {two-colons} env``.

xref:Eval_prog[Eval_prog: ``⊢ command ⊣ %``]

. Let xref:Eval_command[``· ⊢ command ⊣ env``].
. Result in ``env``.

xref:Run_prog[Run_prog: ``⊢ command ⊣ %``]

. If xref:Check_prog[``⊢ command``] holds:
 .. Let xref:Eval_prog[``⊢ command ⊣ env``].
 .. Result in ``env``.
